  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"[the author] translates Scott Joplin's written piano score into a visual scaffolding onto which notes and tones are assigned specific colors and densities. Grouping of notes and rhythmic silences determine both positive and negative spaces. The grid is an integral component of the work since it is the equivalent of the treble and bass staffs modified into four spaces and three lines.... Banks' intention is not for her viewers to 'read' these scores in literal fashion, but rather to focus on the visual play of tumbling notes and color, the negative/positive spaces which are created, and the resulting chromatic harmonies." -- Colophon.</subfield>
  </datafield>
